        "original_id": "77e628dc-9a95-50cd-9edd-089965c67aea",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Organizations: Cosmos\n- People: Jānis Šipkēvics, Andris Sējāns, Juris Lisenko, Jānis Ozols, Jānis Strazdiņš, Reinis Sējāns\n- Places: Riga, Latvia\n- Products: Pa un par\n- Companies: UPE\n- Concepts: bass, classical male singing voice, voice types\n\nFacts:\n- Cosmos was a Latvian a cappella band that formed in Riga in 2002.\n- Cosmos comprised Jānis Šipkēvics and Andris Sējāns as countertenors, Juris Lisenko as tenor, Jānis Ozols as baritone, Jānis Strazdiņš as bass, and Reinis Sējāns as rhythm.\n- In 2005, Cosmos released the album \"Pa un par\" on the UPE record label.\n- A bass is a type of classical male singing voice with the lowest vocal range among voice types.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
